<%doc>

=head1 NAME

/util/app_stepper.mas - numbered step bar of an app page (see /util/app_layout.mas)

=head1 ARGS

steps: arrayref of step titles; id: id of the <ol>;
first: number of the first step in data-step (0 or 1; default 0);
active: data-step of the current step (default: the first).
Steps before the active one are marked done. The page's JavaScript handles
clicks (each <li> has data-step) and moves the active/done/off classes
(off = faded, e.g. an optional step that is not used).

=head1 EXAMPLE

  <& /util/app_stepper.mas, id => 'my_steps', first => 1, steps => ['Data', 'Model', 'Results'] &>

=cut

</%doc>
<%args>
$steps
$first => 0
$active => undef
$id => ''
</%args>
% $active //= $first;
<ol class="bb-stepper"<% $id ? ' id="' . $m->interp->apply_escapes($id, 'h') . '"' : '' %>>
% for my $i (0 .. $#$steps) {
%   my $n = $i + $first;
  <li data-step="<% $n %>" class="<% $n == $active ? 'active' : $n < $active ? 'done' : '' %>"><span class="bb-step-num"><% $i + 1 %></span><span class="bb-step-label"><% $steps->[$i] |h %></span></li>
% }
</ol>
